      m_Calls: []
  m_text: At the centre of the scene, we have a glass ball in the shape of a sphere.
    In front of this ball, we have the camera, and behind it we have the deformed
    object. The deformed object sits behind the camera. Since in this case the original
    object would also have to be there to make the calculation. By clicking on "Fly
    to camera" in the "Ray Tracer" panel, we will be seeing just the sphere ball
    from the perspective of the camera (viewer). The refraction visible, however,
    should look like the original object behind it. To see the image without the
    pixel grid in front of it, click on "Render image".
